  "original_source_bytes_preserved": true,
  "runtime_map_modified": false,
  "runtime_character_modified": false,
  "visual_review": "Continuing from `63cfd9a`, the retained skin texture now has a separate fine pore-relief layer. Hand-specific fields follow the original anatomical joints for crease relief and restrained color variation. A small editable vascular shape control adds back-of-hand definition with matching subdued pigment. Ten closed nail-fold surfaces follow the actual skin beside the proximal nail edges and inherit the original skin UVs. Face and hand scattering/specular response have been adjusted in the native materials.",
  "body_detail_review": "Front, profile and hand studies were rendered, including a closer hand inspection. The first view did not establish whether the small crease detail was seated correctly, so the macro view was used to inspect it before adding restrained vascular definition. The saved-scene checks retain the original nail-plate clearance and require ten closed, outward nail folds seated partly into the skin. Maximum vascular relief is about 0.192 mm; fold vertices range from about 0.095 mm beneath to 0.185 mm above the hand surface. Pore relief remains a procedural shader layer over the unchanged photographic color map; it is not a scanned displacement map or a claim of photographic realism.",
  "remaining": "The full human-realism goal remains active. Fine hand and skin cues are improved, but facial expression, sparse brows and broad cloth folds still make the figure look synthetic. Next develop more natural brow/eyelid presentation and facial expression, then continue garment surface refinement and whole-figure review. Architecture/retail variety and planting remain after human acceptance. Preserve the editable native source and original licenses; this checkpoint changes offline art, not a runtime character or animation rig.",
